(A. Hypertensive Urgency \(Severe Elevation WITHOUT Target Organ Damage\):) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 395 Td
(  * SBP >180 mmHg and/or DBP >120 mmHg with NO acute symptoms of organ failure.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 382 Td
(  * Action: Rest for 5 minutes, repeat measurement. If sustained, contact physician within 24-48 hours.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 369 Td
(  * Does not typically require ICU admission; managed with oral antihypertensive regimen adjustments.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
0.15 0.2 0.3 rg
50 356 Td
(B. Hypertensive Emergency \(Severe Elevation WITH Target Organ Damage\):) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 343 Td
(  * SBP >180 mmHg and/or DBP >120 mmHg WITH acute, life-threatening target organ damage.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 330 Td
(  * Symptoms: Crushing chest pain, severe dyspnea, facial droop, dysarthria, focal weakness, blurred vision.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 317 Td
(  * Action: IMMEDIATE 911 / 997 EMERGENCY CALL. Requires ICU admission and titratable intravenous therapy.) Tj
ET
