(4. Standardized 6-Step Home Blood Pressure Monitoring \(HBPM\) Protocol) Tj
ET
q 0.7 0.75 0.8 rg 45 277 522 0.75 re f Q
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 263 Td
(1. 30-Minute Pre-Test Abstinence: No caffeine \(coffee/tea/energy drinks\), tobacco, or vigorous exercise.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 250 Td
(2. Bladder Emptying: Fully empty bladder prior to reading \(full bladder adds 10-15 mmHg artifact\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 237 Td
(3. 5-Minute Seated Rest: Sit quietly in a comfortable chair in a quiet room; do not speak or use smartphone.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 224 Td
(4. Correct Anatomical Posture: Back supported, feet flat on the floor \(uncrossed; crossing adds 5-8 mmHg\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 211 Td
(5. Arm & Cuff Alignment: Arm supported on a table so that the cuff center is at EXACT HEART LEVEL.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
50 198 Td
(6. Bare Skin & Proper Cuff Size: Place cuff on bare upper arm; small cuff overestimates BP by up to 10 mmHg.) Tj
ET
